---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import EveryCut from '../../components/EveryCut.astro';
import GuideData from '../../components/GuideData.astro';
import {bySlug,kicker} from '../../dossiers/registry.js';
import {investorModel} from '../../dossiers/investor-participation.model.js';
import {investorFormat} from '../../dossiers/investor-participation.format.js';
import {serializeInvestorPayload} from '../../dossiers/investor-participation.payload.js';
const D=bySlug['investor-participation'],model=investorModel();
const period=date=>new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-IN',{month:'long',year:'numeric',timeZone:'UTC'}).format(new Date(date+'T00:00:00Z'));
const asOf=model.facts.find(f=>f.id==='aum')?.date;
if(!asOf)throw Error('Investor guide requires a reviewed month-end assets headline');
---
<Base title={`${D.title} · India Atlas`} description={D.description} nav="guides" dateStamp={period(asOf)} crumbLeft='<a href="/guides/">Guides</a> / Markets / <b>Investor participation</b>' crumbRight={`${D.statusNote}, <b>${D.version}</b>`} canonical="https://atlas.thisindianlife.today/guides/investor-participation/" ogImage="/og/investor-participation.png">
<div class="page">
 <div class="titleblock break" data-inputs={model.plates.map(p=>p.bundle).join(', ')} data-prose="evergreen and data-bound facts">
  <div class="kicker">{kicker(D)}</div><div class="hero-grid"><h1 set:html={D.headline}/><p class="lede">Mutual fund disclosures describe money entering and leaving schemes, the assets held, and the records used to administer investments. Each measure has its own definition and reference period.</p></div>
  <div class="meta"><span>Reviewed conventional fund report <b>{period(asOf)}</b></span><span id="prov-vintage">Source revision date: not published.</span><span>Sources <b>AMFI and SEBI</b></span></div>
  <div class="numbers" data-long-values>{model.facts.map(f=><div class="num"><div class="l">{f.label}</div><div class="v" id={'n-'+f.id}>{investorFormat(f.value,f.unit)}</div><div class="d">{period(f.date)}</div></div>)}</div>
 </div>
 <section data-prose="evergreen"><div class="sec-head"><h2>What the measures describe</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="reading-cols"><div class="reading-col"><p>A purchase adds money to a scheme. Redeeming units takes money out. Net inflow subtracts the reported redemptions from money received. The value of investments already held also moves with market prices, so changes in asset values do not measure new subscriptions.</p><p>Month-end assets value holdings at the reporting date. Average assets describe the source’s measure across the named month. Keep their time bases visible when reading them.</p></div><div class="reading-col"><p>Industry disclosures include institutional investors as well as individuals. Asset values do not tell us the fraction of households investing, their median portfolio size or their financial security.</p><p><a href="/guides/markets/">Savings, markets and companies</a> places fund disclosures alongside the wider financial accounts. Those sources use separate instruments and definitions.</p></div></div></section>
 <section data-prose="methodology"><div class="sec-head"><h2>Source review and access</h2><span class="line"></span></div><p>The charts below show source columns whose units, reference periods and original workbook cells have been reviewed. Other source records remain listed in the complete register with their review status. A pending record is retained in the archival download; it is not used for a chart, headline, comparison or derived rate.</p><p>The conventional monthly report places domestic funds of funds in a separate informational memo because their underlying schemes already include those assets. The source’s grand total is used directly. The average-assets header establishes the named monthly measure; this review does not establish the source’s arithmetic averaging method.</p></section>
 {model.plates.map(p=><section data-inputs={p.bundle} data-prose="source definition and data-bound readings"><div class="break"><figure id={'cb-'+p.id} data-quality-policy={p.sourceQuality.id}>
  <div class="investor-graphic"><div class="plate-head"><div class="t"><h3>{p.title}</h3><div class="sub">{p.sub}</div></div><div class="plate-val"><div class="v" id={'pv-'+p.id}>{investorFormat(p.rows[0].value,p.unit)}</div><div class="c">{p.period}</div></div></div>
  <div class="frame"><div class="plotzone"><div id={'plot-'+p.id} data-investor-plot></div></div><div class="plotfoot"><span class="src">{p.source.meta.source}, {p.period}. {p.sourceQuality.definition}</span><span class="dl"><button type="button" data-dl="svg">SVG</button><button type="button" data-dl="png">PNG</button><button type="button" data-dl="csv">CSV</button><a href={p.sourceUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Source ↗</a></span></div><p data-export-status aria-live="polite"></p></div>
  </div><div class="explain"><div class="ev"><span class="mk">How to read this</span><p>{p.explain}</p></div><div class="now"><span class="mk">Source observations</span><p>{p.sourceQuality.referenceBasis}</p></div></div>
  <table class="investor-source-table"><caption>{p.title}: published observations</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Reference period</th><th scope="col">{p.unit==='inr_crore'?'Value, ₹ crore':'Value, '+p.unit}</th></tr></thead><tbody>{p.source.dates.map((date,i)=><tr><th scope="row">{p.periodLabels[date]}</th><td>{investorFormat(p.source.record.data[i],p.unit)}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table>
 </figure></div></section>)}
 <EveryCut slug="investor-participation"/><GuideData slug="investor-participation"/>
 <section data-inputs={model.bundles.join(', ')} data-prose="methodology"><div class="sec-head"><h2>Sources, method and revisions</h2><span class="line"></span></div><p>AMFI and SEBI products remain separate source instruments. The register preserves older classifications, reference periods, source labels, negative entries and missing observations. Canonical dates are period keys; an asset stock refers to its source reporting date rather than the first day shown in that key.</p><p>Source revision timestamps are unknown. Archive capture, publication edition and reference period remain separate. Earlier AMFI layouts and PDF or HTML releases, older SEBI PDF-only issues and unparsed launch-report sheets remain unfinished extraction. Their availability does not establish complete canonical coverage.</p><p><a href="https://www.amfiindia.com/research-information/amfi-data">AMFI publications</a>. <a href="https://www.sebi.gov.in/sebiweb/home/HomeAction.do?doListing=yes&amp;sid=4&amp;ssid=80&amp;smid=107">SEBI Monthly Bulletin</a>.</p></section>
</div>
<script is:inline type="application/json" id="investor-participation-data" data-quality-version={model.qualityVersion} set:html={serializeInvestorPayload(model.payload)}/>
<script>import '../../dossiers/investor-participation.client.js';import '../../dossiers/guide.client.js';</script>
<style>
 .investor-source-table{width:100%;table-layout:fixed;overflow-wrap:anywhere;margin:24px 0;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.investor-source-table th,.investor-source-table td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;padding:8px 12px}.investor-source-table caption{text-align:left;font-size:12px;color:#4A5160}.investor-source-table td{text-align:right}
 @media print{.investor-graphic{break-inside:avoid;page-break-inside:avoid;padding-top:8px}.investor-source-table{display:table!important;break-inside:avoid}.dl,[data-export-status]{display:none!important}[data-investor-plot]{break-inside:avoid}}
</style>
